+# The estate's pools of pull-request runners, and what a runner in any of
+# them reaches to be a runner at all: to be handed a job, fetch the actions
+# it names, and send back its log and what it made.
+#
+# A pull request's job on the estate's own runners is held by the cluster's
+# network and not by an agent in the runner. A pool is held to what the jobs
+# declared for it below reach between them, and to this, and to nothing
+# else; tests/go/repo holds each pool's policy to exactly that. Each job
+# says which pool it is of with `pool:` beside its entry under egress:.
+#
+# The last of these is wide and cannot be narrowed: the platform keeps logs
+# and artifacts in storage accounts it names as it goes.
+pull_request_pools:
+  names:
